  "id": "COMPOUND:30160 - PROTEIN:4284",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound [(3S,9S,12R,13R,14R,15R)-13-hydroxy-6-(1-hydroxyethyl)-12,14-dimethyl-2,5,8,11-tetraoxo-9-(propan-2-yl)-15-tridecyl-1-oxa-4,7,10-triazacyclopentadecan-3-yl]methyl acetate and Vascular endothelial growth factor B (VEGF-B). This compound is identified as a target for multiple drugs, including K-252a, which is known to inhibit VEGF-B through a mechanism involving the suppression of its signaling. The compound also acts as a target for dual specificity protein kinase CLK2 and Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which are involved in the transport and regulation of VEGF-B. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may exert its effects by modulating the activity of key regulators of VEGF-B, potentially through interactions with the signaling pathways that control its expression and function. The consistent presence of the compound as a target for multiple drugs, along with the documented mode of action of K-252a, supports the hypothesis that the compound may play a role in the regulation of VEGF-B, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
